*.pdf
*.ipynb

# Python build and cache artifacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Docs build output (ProperDocs)
site/

# Local run scratch, one root for every tier (runs/probes, runs/physics,
# runs/drift, runs/fsi, campaign workspaces); the committed evidence is
# the reports/ tree, never the scratch. Convention recorded at HND-035
# session close; the earlier per-tier roots (probe_runs/, physics_runs/,
# drift_runs*/, fsi_runs/) moved under runs/ the same day.
runs/

# LaTeX build artifacts of the beamer guide; the built pdf never
# enters Git (repository guard), only guide/*.tex is committed
guide/*.pdf
guide/*.aux
guide/*.log
guide/*.nav
guide/*.out
guide/*.snm
guide/*.toc
guide/*.fls
guide/*.fdb_latexmk
guide/*.synctex.gz
guide/*.vrb

# Local machine configuration. Absolute paths locating local tooling live
# here and nowhere else: `tests/test_house_style.py` refuses a user-profile
# path or a workspace-container path in any COMMITTED file, and this is the
# gitignored home that exemption assumes.
.claude/settings.local.json

# A NESTED SECOND CHECKOUT, if one is ever parked inside this tree, belongs
# here too and the reason is measured rather than tidy: the shipped-surface
# scan builds its inventory from `git ls-files` PLUS
# `--others --exclude-standard`, and turns any path it cannot read into a
# refusal rather than a skip. An unignored scratch checkout therefore fails
# tier 1 with a message about coverage holes, and the cause reads as a
# checker defect. Keep it out of the style walk by absolute PREFIX rather
# than by directory name; `tests/test_house_style.py` records above its own
# `SKIP_DIRS` how a name once blanked that walk entirely.

# Coverage data and reports (NFR-16). The measurement is a local
# artifact; the FLOOR it is checked against is versioned, in
# pyproject.toml's [tool.coverage.report].
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
# The role-review push gate's audit record, and this repository PUBLISHES, so
# the line matters more here than anywhere else. role_review_gate.py DENIES a
# push from pyflightstream until an attestation covers every commit it makes
# new, and the remedy it prints writes that record to
# <repo root>/.claude/.role_review_attestation.json. It names review lenses and
# commit shas: an argument for a push, never release content, and never
# something a wheel should carry. Only `.claude/settings.local.json` was
# ignored above, so before this line the gate's own remedy left a stageable
# audit file in a tree that ships. The path is duplicated in
# role_review_gate.py, write_attestation.py and here; a rename must touch all
# three, and check_hook_provenance.py asserts that it does, in every repository
# the gate can write into.
.claude/.role_review_attestation.json
# AND THE DIRECTORY, because ignoring only the file was half the fix.
# 83db2f2 ignored the attestation so it could not be staged into a tree
# that ships, and left `.claude/` itself neither tracked nor ignored. The
# root-artifact guard in tests/test_examples.py closes its question the
# other way round: a path at the root is accounted for when git tracks it
# OR ignores it, and anything else is something a run left behind. So the
# first attestation this repository ever wrote turned that guard red while
# the file inside it was correctly ignored.
#
# Ignoring the directory is the deliberate half. Nothing under `.claude/`
# is tracked here: the process tooling left this repository in 158f5de,
# and what remains is the gate's own local write target. Anything that
# should ship from here does not belong under `.claude/`.
.claude/

# The agent instruction file is the author's WORKING METHOD and is not a
# product of this library. It was tracked on a PUBLIC remote until
# 2026-08-25 and is untracked from here: the file stays on disk so a
# session still loads it, and stops being published.
#
# NOTE, because removing a path from HEAD is not the same as unpublishing
# it: every commit before this one still carries the file, and the public
# history is unchanged. Taking it out of the history is a rewrite and a
# force push, which is the author's decision and not a side effect of
# this change.
CONTRIBUTING.md
